Theorem DP-5: can_mutate_in_place — alias-safety with SetTag invalidation + project_alias_sources 7-rule envelope

  Preconditions:
    - s is a canonical AimsState per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
    - can_mutate_in_place :
        AimsState x ArcVarId x FieldPath x ProgramPoint -> Bool
      per Annex E §AIMS DP-5 + Appendix C truth table
    - DP-5 is context-dependent — it consults THREE side-table / liveness
      inputs in addition to AimsState:
        (i) borrow_sources (per Annex E §AIMS.9) — direct
              borrow tracker populated by TF-4 Project; entry shape
              { source: ArcVarId, path: FieldPath } per ArcVarId
        (ii) project_alias_sources (per Annex E §AIMS.9) —
              transitive alias tracker; ArcVarId -> SmallVec ArcVarId
              constructed under 7 rules (R1 Direct, R2 Let, R3 Jump-arg,
              R4 CFG-merge, R5 Select, R6 Transitive-nested-Project,
              R7 Set/SetTag preserves prior sources)
        (iii) live-variable set at the mutation ProgramPoint
    - InstructionKind in {Set, SetTag} — DP-5 must enforce RL-10 SetTag
      invalidation: a tag change invalidates ALL payload fields (variant
      may have different layout) -> DP-5 treats SetTag as overlapping
      every field, regardless of borrow path
    - DP-5 is the SOLE decision predicate requiring the typed pre-pass
      inputs (i) + (ii) + (iii) per Annex E §AIMS DP-5 +
      the proof-checker design Engine-per-Category-Inventory
      DP-row
    - project_alias_sources shipped surface per Annex E §AIMS.9
      partial-shipment envelope: rules R1, R2, R3, R4, R6 shipped; R5
      (Select) and R7 (Set/SetTag mutation tracking) target-only. The
      proof discharges across the FULL 7-rule envelope, including the
      target-only rules (no deferral of target-only obligations).

  Soundness property:
    Forall (s, var, field, point, instruction_kind).
      can_mutate_in_place(s, var, field, point, instruction_kind)
        <=> (s.access = O
              AND s.uniqueness = u
              AND no_active_overlapping_borrows(var, field, point,
                                                instruction_kind))

    where no_active_overlapping_borrows decomposes into:

      Step 1 — Direct borrow check (over borrow_sources):
        For every b such that borrow_sources.b.source = var:
          if b is live at point AND
             (instruction_kind = SetTag
              OR overlaps(borrow_sources.b.path, field))
          then overlap = true
        overlaps(p1, p2) = (p1 is a prefix of p2 OR p2 is a prefix of
        p1). Disjoint = NOT overlaps.

      Step 2 — Transitive alias check (over project_alias_sources):
        For every a such that var in project_alias_sources.a
          AND a not in { b : borrow_sources.b.source = var }:
          if a is live at point
          then alias_block = true
        Non-borrow aliases lack field-level granularity; ANY live
        non-borrow alias blocks conservatively.

      no_active_overlapping_borrows = NOT overlap AND NOT alias_block.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Exhaustive enumeration over the Appendix C DP-5 5-row truth
          table, with two orthogonal axes added — instruction_kind in
          {Set, SetTag} and the §AIMS §7 7-rule envelope coverage axis.
      (b) Soundness equality on every enumerated case + side-table
          invariants (RL-10 SetTag whole-payload + R5 + R7 target-only
          rules) discharge against the explicit per-row truth.

    Part (a) — Appendix C DP-5 row partition (5 rows, exhaustive):
      Row 1: Access != O, any Uniqueness, any borrow state, any alias
        state -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (first conjunct s.access = O fails).
        Borrowed values never own their RC; in-place mutation would
        violate the borrowed alias contract.

      Row 2: Access = O, Uniqueness != u (MaybeShared OR Shared), any
        borrow state, any alias state -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (second conjunct s.uniqueness = u
        fails). DP-9 distinguishes the MaybeShared and Shared sub-cases
        via cow_mode (Dynamic / StaticShared respectively); DP-5
        returns false uniformly. This is the negative-direction witness
        for the Uniqueness gate — RC > 1 risk forbids unconditional
        in-place mutation.

      Row 3: Access = O, Uniqueness = u, direct borrow overlaps field
        at point (instruction_kind respected for SetTag whole-payload
        semantics), any alias state -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (third conjunct
        no_active_overlapping_borrows fails via Step 1). RC = 1 but
        mutation would corrupt the borrowed view; disjoint-field RL-10
        exemption does NOT apply when the borrow path overlaps the
        mutation field (neither is prefix of the other excludes the
        non-overlap case).

      Row 4: Access = O, Uniqueness = u, no direct overlap, AT LEAST
        ONE live transitive alias (R2 / R3 / R4 / R5 / R6 / R7) -> false
        Soundness: predicate false (third conjunct fails via Step 2).
        Aliases lack field-level granularity per Annex E §AIMS.9;
        any live non-borrow alias blocks conservatively.

      Row 5: Access = O, Uniqueness = u, no direct overlap, no live
        transitive alias -> true
        Soundness: predicate true (all three conjuncts hold). RC = 1 +
        no active borrow conflict -> in-place mutation safe.

    Part (a.1) — SetTag invalidation clause (per Annex E §AIMS
    RL-10 + sec-3 TF-15a):
      For instruction_kind = SetTag, EVERY direct borrow on var that is
      live at point overlaps (regardless of borrow field path). Reason:
      SetTag changes the enum discriminant; the payload layout may
      differ across variants; reading any borrowed field after the tag
      change is undefined. DP-5 SHALL treat SetTag as overlapping every
      field path.

      SetTag truth-table sub-rows (composed with Rows 1-5 above):
        SetTag + O + u + any-live-direct-borrow -> false (Row 3)
        SetTag + O + u + no-direct-borrow + any-live-alias -> false (Row 4)
        SetTag + O + u + no-direct-borrow + no-live-alias -> true (Row 5)

      The verifier enumerates the SetTag axis explicitly + confirms
      RL-10 forces overlap = true on every (live-direct-borrow x any-
      field-path) combination.

    Part (a.2) — project_alias_sources 7-rule envelope coverage:
      The proof discharges across all 7 alias-construction rules per
      Annex E §AIMS.9:

        R1 (Direct Project) — SHIPPED (composes with sec-04
                                       IA-5 step (1) borrow-rules subset)
        R2 (Let aliases) — SHIPPED
        R3 (Jump-arg block-param) — SHIPPED
        R4 (CFG merge union) — SHIPPED
        R5 (Select aliases) — TARGET-ONLY (this proof discharges
                                       the target-only obligation; no
                                       deferral)
        R6 (Transitive nested-Project) — SHIPPED
        R7 (Set/SetTag preserves prior sources) — TARGET-ONLY (this
                                       proof discharges the obligation)

      project_alias_sources envelope summary:
        shipped: R1, R2, R3, R4, R6
        target_only_proven_here: R5, R7

      Per-rule discharge witness (each rule contribution to the alias
      set is exercised by the verifier enumeration over alias-origin
      kinds):
        R1: dst = Project src.field -> dst in
              project_alias_sources.dst-origin-R1 traces to src (and
              borrow_sources also records the direct borrow). DP-5
              Step 1 catches this case for overlap; Step 2 NOT triggered
              (R1 entries ALSO appear in borrow_sources).
        R2: y = Let Var(x) where x has alias set S -> y maps to
              [x] union S. Step 2 catches a live y when x not in
              borrow_sources for var.
        R3: Jump block1, args = [x]; block1 params [p] -> p maps to
              [x] union sources(x). Step 2 catches a live p
              referencing var through x chain.
        R4: CFG-merge union over predecessor alias entries -> Step 2
              catches any live merged alias.
        R5: y = Select(cond, A, B) -> y maps to [A, B] union
              sources(A) union sources(B). Step 2 catches a live y
              referencing var through A or B.
        R6: z = Project y.field2 where y has alias set S -> z maps to
              [y] union S. Step 2 catches a live z transitively
              referencing var through y; Step 1 catches the direct
              borrow on y.field2 only when its source = var.
        R7: Set / SetTag — base preserves prior sources, NO new alias
              created. Step 1 catches direct borrows on base; Step 2
              catches the preserved aliases via base prior alias set.

      The 7-rule envelope is exhaustive per §AIMS §7 — no construction
      rule omitted.

    Part (b) — Coverage gate:
      Per the verifier section_05::verify_dp5_can_mutate_in_place_with_settag:
        Pure-lattice axis: 2 Access x 3 Uniqueness = 6 base states.
        instruction_kind axis: 2 (Set, SetTag).
        Direct-borrow axis: 3 (none, live-overlap, live-disjoint).
          Note: SetTag forces overlap regardless of stated path; the
          verifier expands this axis to enforce RL-10.
        Transitive-alias axis: 2 (none-live, any-live).
        Coverage product: 6 x 2 x 3 x 2 = 72 enumerated cases per the
        Appendix C row partition + RL-10 SetTag + R5 + R7 envelope.

      Row 5 (true partition) canonical-case enumeration:
        O x u x (no-overlap) x (no-live-alias) x (instruction_kind):
          (O, u, Set, none, none-live) -> true
          (O, u, Set, live-disjoint, none-live) -> true (RL-10 disjoint exemption)
          (O, u, SetTag, none, none-live) -> true
        SetTag + live-disjoint is FALSE because SetTag invalidates all
        fields. Total: 3 true cases.
      Rows 1-4 (false partition) canonical-case enumeration: balance of
        the product; the verifier enumerates exhaustively and confirms
        soundness equality on each.

    Negative-direction witness — MaybeShared + no-borrow + no-alias
    counterexample:
      Consider s = (O, L, 1, ms, bl, R-S, NONE); no direct borrow on
      var; no transitive alias live. Per the predicate s.uniqueness =
      ms violates second conjunct -> DP-5 = false. Per Appendix C
      Row 2 the same case yields false. Sound: RC may be > 1; DP-9
      routes the same configuration to Dynamic (runtime IsShared check)
      per row (d) — DP-5 alone cannot license in-place mutation.

    Negative-direction witness — Unique + live-overlapping-direct-borrow:
      Consider s = (O, L, 1, u, bl, Phi, NONE); direct borrow b with
      borrow_sources.b.source = var and borrow_sources.b.path
      overlapping the mutation field; b live at point. Per the
      predicate Step 1 sets overlap = true ->
      no_active_overlapping_borrows = false -> DP-5 = false. Per
      Appendix C Row 3 the same case yields false. Sound: RC = 1 but
      borrowed view would observe corrupt state post-mutation.

    Negative-direction witness — Unique + SetTag + any-live-direct-borrow:
      Consider s = (O, L, 1, u, bl, R-E, NONE); instruction_kind =
      SetTag; direct borrow b with borrow_sources.b.source = var,
      borrow_sources.b.path = any field; b live at point. Per RL-10
      SetTag forces overlap = true regardless of b field path -> Step
      1 returns block -> DP-5 = false. Sound: tag change invalidates
      ALL payload fields per sec-3 TF-15a + sec-8 RL-10; any live
      borrow blocks in-place mutation.

    Negative-direction witness — Unique + live R5 Select alias + no
    direct borrow + Set:
      Consider y = Select(cond, A, B); A is the projection root
      tracking var; y live at point; no entry b with
      borrow_sources.b.source = var. Per project_alias_sources R5
      y in project_alias_sources.y-origin-R5 maps to [A, B] union ...;
      Step 2 finds y live + var in its alias set + y not in
      borrow_sources for var -> alias_block = true ->
      no_active_overlapping_borrows = false -> DP-5 = false. Sound:
      conservatively blocks; no field-level disambiguation possible
      for Select aliases.

    Positive-direction witness — Unique + disjoint-field-borrow + Set:
      Consider src holds a struct with two fields { x, y }; a borrow
      b1 = Project(src, x) is live; mutation is Set(src.y, ...). Per
      RL-10 disjoint-field exemption + Step 1 overlaps(x, y) = false
      (neither prefix of the other) -> overlap = false. No live
      transitive alias on src -> alias_block = false ->
      no_active_overlapping_borrows = true. Per predicate DP-5 = true.
      Sound: borrowed view of x unaffected by mutation of y; RC = 1.

    project_alias_sources envelope declaration:
      shipped: R1, R2, R3, R4, R6
      target_only_proven_here: R5, R7
      composes_with: aims-proof/proofs/04-transfers/IA-5-step-1.proof
                     for the BORROW-rule subset (R1 + R6).

    Live-variable / borrow_sources / project_alias_sources typed
    pre-pass dependency: REQUIRED for DP-5 (DP-5 is the SOLE decision
    predicate that consults these typed pre-pass inputs per Annex E §AIMS DP-5 + the proof-checker design DP-row line 99).
    The verifier constructs synthetic side-table fixtures covering each
    row of the Appendix C truth table + RL-10 SetTag + R5 + R7
    envelope; the fixture suite is encoded in
    section_05::verify_dp5_can_mutate_in_place_with_settag.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix C 5-row enumeration + RL-10
        SetTag whole-payload invalidation axis + §AIMS §7 7-rule
        envelope axis per section_05::verify_dp5_can_mutate_in_place_with_settag;
        the verifier checks the soundness equality predicate-vs-row-
        partition on every enumerated case and emits Fail on any
        divergence)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_05 case_analysis engine discharges DP-5 via 72-case enumeration over (Access x Uniqueness x instruction_kind x direct-borrow-state x transitive-alias-state) covering Appendix C 5-row truth table + RL-10 SetTag whole-payload invalidation + §AIMS §7 7-rule alias-construction envelope (R1-R7) per Annex E §AIMS DP-5 + Appendix C + sec-8 RL-10
